*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.usd.bak
.scratch/

# The fourth nav scene, and the ONLY one of the four kept out of git, because it references
# the TIC-VLA submodule by absolute path and resolves to nothing on anyone else's machine.
#
# History worth keeping: until 2026-09-10 this file was a 44-line STUB. The first build
# crashed after step 1 had saved the layer, and bench.sh treated the stub as a cached stage,
# so every outdoor run before the 09-10 rebuild drove a robot with no joint drives, no wheel
# colliders and no camera_nav. build_nav_scene.sh now builds into a temporary file and
# renames it into place only after all four steps succeed. The km-scale outdoor paths that
# continued AFTER the rebuild were a separate bug -- the kinematic base never wrote root
# velocity, see nav/sim/base_drive.py -- fixed 2026-10-05.
assets/usd/nav_outdoor_small.usda
# In-progress nav stage builds (nav/sim/build_nav_scene.sh renames one into place only
# after all four steps succeed). One left behind means a build was killed outright.
assets/usd/.nav_*.build-*.usda
assets/usd/.nav_*.build-*.log

# Local Claude Code settings, and Springer's template distribution (not ours to publish).
.claude/
midi_conference/LaTeX2e+Proceedings+Template+ZIP/
# LaTeX build artifacts of the paper. main.bbl stays tracked, for Overleaf and arXiv.
midi_conference/qvla_paper/*.aux
midi_conference/qvla_paper/*.blg
midi_conference/qvla_paper/*.out
midi_conference/qvla_paper/DescriptionTexts.txt
# Derived from NVIDIA's pretrained Isaac Lab G1 checkpoint on the Omniverse content CDN,
# whose redistribution terms have not been checked. Regenerate with
# nav/tools/g1_export_policy.py (its docstring has the source URL and the command).
nav/sim/g1/data/policy/*.npz
*.orig
